{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q408908","formula":"C₃H₄N₂","hill":"C3H4N2","elements":["H","C","N"],"composition":{"C":3.0,"H":4.0,"N":2.0},"names":{"en":"Pyrazole","ru":"Пиразол","uk":"Піразол"},"descriptions":{"en":"Pyrazole is an organic compound with the formula (CH)3N2H. It is a heterocycle characterized as an azole with a 5-membered ring of three carbon atoms and two adjacent nitrogen atoms, which are in ortho-substitution. Pyrazoles are also a class of compounds that have the ring C3N2 with adjacent nitrogen atoms. Pyrazole itself has few applications but many substituted pyrazoles are of commercial interest.","ru":"Пиразол — пятичленный гетероцикл, аналог пиррола, в котором группировка -СН- в положении 2 заменена на атом азота; изомерен имидазолу.","uk":"Піразо́л (рос. пиразол, англ. pyrazole) — органічна сполука, що є 6π-гетероароматичним п'ятичленним 1,2-діазолом складу C3H4N2."},"fame":31,"pubchemCid":1048,"mass":68.08,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CNN=C1","inchikey":"WTKZEGDFNFYCGP-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1H-pyrazole","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"1048","atoms":9,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.307,"y":1.061,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":1.2,"y":0.057,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.992,"y":0.644,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.945,"y":-0.728,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":0.429,"y":-1.034,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.813,"y":1.346,"z":0.0,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.784,"y":-1.408,"z":0.0,"el":"H"},{"x":0.655,"y":2.012,"z":0.0,"el":"H"},{"x":0.901,"y":-2.006,"z":0.0,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,1,1],[0,2,1],[0,7,1],[1,4,2],[2,3,2],[2,5,1],[3,4,1],[3,6,1],[4,8,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q408908","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pyrazole","license":"CC BY-S